NAME
    wmedit - text editor WM client (Path C phase 30)

SYNOPSIS
    wmedit [PATH] [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 640x400 editor window over the file at PATH (defaults
    to /tmp/edit if omitted).  Missing files open as empty
    buffers — Ctrl+S creates them on first save.  SECONDS is
    the lifetime cap (default 600 = 10 minutes); Ctrl+Q exits
    early.

    Keys (only delivered when the window has keyboard focus —
    click into the window first):
      printable ASCII   insert at cursor
      Enter             insert newline
      Backspace / DEL   delete char before cursor
      Tab               insert 4 spaces
      Arrow keys        move cursor up/down/left/right
      Ctrl+S            save buffer to PATH
      Ctrl+Q            quit
      Ctrl+C            copy entire buffer to the global clipboard
      Ctrl+V            paste clipboard contents at the cursor

    Mouse: clicking in the text region positions the cursor on
    the row/col under the click.

    The window title shows "wmedit  Ctrl-S save  Ctrl-Q quit"
    when focused.  The bottom status bar shows the path, a
    [*] marker if there are unsaved edits, and the current
    cursor position as "L<row>:<col> B<total-bytes>".

LIMITATIONS
    Single 8 KiB buffer cap.  No selection, search, undo, or
    file picker — those are future polish.  Arrow-key support
    relies on the kernel's ANSI CSI passthrough for arrows
    (ESC '[' A/B/C/D), same path the shell uses for history
    navigation.

SEE ALSO
    wmtype(1), wmterm(1), wmd(1)
